# tooling/regression/regression.env — harness infrastructure config for the mbirtorch nightly
# regression.
#
# CANONICAL HOME: this harness lives in and runs from the mbirtorch_metrics repo, so edit it
# here.  Each nightly run updates a persistent metrics clone and re-execs from it (see WORK_DIR),
# so remote harness, config, and state changes are always picked up and no per-node path is baked
# in.
#
# The user-facing run knobs (tracked branches, the torch wheel index, the SLURM request) live in
# action_scripts/run_configs.env, sourced just below.  Everything in THIS file is infrastructure:
# URLs, paths, credentials, and the schedule.  Sourced as bash.

source "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/../../action_scripts/run_configs.env"

ENABLED=1                       # master kill-switch (0 = installed but the wrapper exits
                                # immediately; prefer enable_nightly / disable_nightly)

# FIRE-ON-CHANGE: the wrapper wakes on POLL_SCHEDULE, reads each TRACKED_BRANCHES tip via
# `git ls-remote`, and measures a branch ONLY when it differs from the last-measured commit
# recorded in state/<plat>/.
#
# 03:00 is one hour after the mbirjax nightly, which runs on the same cluster from its own
# repository.  Slurm allocates the two jobs separately and they write to different repositories,
# so the stagger is insurance against queueing contention, not a correctness requirement.
POLL_SCHEDULE="0 3 * * *"

# (macOS runs at MACOS_NIGHTLY_TIME from run_configs.env; POLL_SCHEDULE is cluster-only.)

# ── Repos (URLs, not paths — the harness clones both itself) ──────────────────────────────────
METRICS_URL="https://github.com/cabouman/mbirtorch_metrics.git"   # harness + results + state
MBIRTORCH_URL="https://github.com/cabouman/mbirtorch.git"         # library under test

# Node-independent scratch for the persistent metrics clone and the throwaway library clones.
# The wrapper uses $WORK_DIR/.lock.d as its single-instance lock and $WORK_DIR/metrics as the
# clone it pushes from, so this directory must belong to this nightly alone.
#   export MBIRTORCH_REGRESSION_WORK="$SCRATCH/mbirtorch_regression"   (honored below)
WORK_DIR="${MBIRTORCH_REGRESSION_WORK:-$HOME/.mbirtorch/regression}"

# ── Build / test ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DEDICATED env — never a development env.  The per-branch editable installs churn the env and
# then delete the clone they point at, and a development env would inherit every experiment as an
# unattributed change to the nightly's measurements.  lib_env.sh creates it if it is missing.
# REG_VENV overrides it with an existing venv for TRIAL runs only.
CONDA_ENV="mbirtorch_regression"
# The HARNESS's own python deps, not mbirtorch's.  scaling_common imports ruamel.yaml at module
# level.  recent_runs.py, which status_nightly.sh calls, reuses the dashboard reader and needs
# PyYAML, so the dedicated env carries that too.  The published dashboard is built by a GitHub
# Action, which installs its own copy.
HARNESS_DEPS="ruamel.yaml pyyaml"
RUN_TESTS=1                     # 1 = run the mbirtorch suite -> tests_<plat>_<date>.txt beside the
                                # run.  The suite carries test_vs_goldens.py, which is the value
                                # check against mbirjax, and the reason the nightly itself has no
                                # cross-framework column.

# ── Node preamble (cluster module loads + proxy) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# A script the wrapper SOURCES in both phases, before any git or conda call.  It must `module
# load` conda, and cuda on GPU, and export HTTPS_PROXY and HTTP_PROXY, because the compute node
# needs the proxy to reach GitHub.  It is sourced, so it must contain module loads and exports
# only, with no `exit` and no `set -e`.  The path below exists only on the cluster, so the
# wrapper's `[ -f ]` guard skips it on the Mac.  See cluster_preamble.sh.example.
PREAMBLE_FILE="$HOME/load_conda_cuda.sh"

# ── Transport / notify ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
MAX_PUSH_FILE_MB=25             # safety cap: the wrapper unstages any oversized result before pushing
# Unattended-push credential (cluster).  A git credential-store file (chmod 600) containing ONE
# line:  https://<github-user>:<fine-grained-PAT>@github.com
# The token must grant write access to cabouman/mbirtorch_metrics.  A token scoped to another
# repository will not work here, so this is a separate file from the mbirjax nightly's.  Create it
# once per cluster node with action_scripts/create_token.sh.  Never commit the file.
TOKEN_FILE="$HOME/.config/mbirtorch/metrics_credentials"
NOTIFY="buzzard@purdue.edu"     # slurm --mail-user for the mbirtorch-nightly job
